        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): dripping inbound media downloads hang past setup timeout",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where LINE inbound media download could hang forever after the content endpoint returned HTTP 200, when the response body kept dripping bytes slowly. `fetchLineContentWhenReady` cleared its 15s `AbortController` after headers returned `Readable.fromWeb(response.body)`, leaving no wall-clock bound on the Node stream consumed by `saveMediaStream` — a slow-drip CDN body would keep inbound media handling alive indefinitely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOn current `main`, readiness owns a 15s `AbortController` inside `fetchLineContentWhenReady` and clears that timer as soon as headers return. After headers, only the Node stream remains — with no wall-clock — so a slow drip can keep `saveMediaStream` alive indefinitely.\n\nThis keeps the existing **15s readiness** contract for 202→retry polling, and adds a separate **120s body** wall-clock after HTTP 200 that aborts and destroys the Node stream via a fresh `AbortController`. Body budget matches Slack/Feishu inbound media totals (`SLACK_MEDIA_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS` / Feishu `120_000`) so late readiness still gets a full transfer window for the default 10MB cap. LINE documents `api-data.line.me` as the large-data content endpoint where video/audio may spend time preparing before binary retrieval.\n\nNon-goals: changing shared `saveMediaStream`, LINE send/API surfaces, or collapsing readiness+body into one shared 15s budget.\n\nCollision check: no open PR on `extensions/line/src/download.ts`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Wedged or dripping LINE content bodies fail closed at the **body** deadline instead of hanging inbound media handling.\n- Healthy media that becomes ready late still gets a full body transfer budget (no longer starved by a shared 15s total).\n- Readiness-only behavior for hung pre-header / endless 202 polling stays at 15s.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `5b8778dd0dc5da81cccac9a432958480461a875a`\n\n`oxfmt --check extensions/line/src/download.ts extensions/line/src/download.test.ts extensions/line/src/download.deadline.loopback.test.ts` — passed.\n`git diff --check` — clean.\n\n### Timeout contract\n\n| Phase | Budget | Scope |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Readiness | `CONTENT_READY_TIMEOUT_MS` = 15s | 202 polling until HTTP 200 headers |\n| Body | `LINE_MEDIA_BODY_TIMEOUT_MS` = 120s | `saveMediaStream` after headers; stream destroyed on abort |\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/line/src/download.test.ts extensions/line/src/download.deadline.loopback.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > persists inbound media with the shared media store 385ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > does not pass the external messageId to saveMediaStream 3ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > cancels content when the media store rejects it 5ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > uses media store content type for M4A media 3ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > passes original filenames to the media store for extension fallback 3ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > uses media store content type for MP4 video 2ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > retries 202 responses and cancels every discarded body 3ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > cancels every response when content never becomes ready 3ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > cancels error responses without retrying 2ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > aborts a hung content request at the readiness deadline 11ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > aborts a dripping content body after headers within the body deadline 62ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.test.ts > downloadLineMedia > keeps a fresh body deadline after late readiness 3ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.deadline.loopback.test.ts > LINE media download wall-clock loopback > aborts a dripping content body within the body wall-clock deadline 692ms\n ✓ |extension-line| extensions/line/src/download.deadline.loopback.test.ts > LINE media download wall-clock loopback > persists a slow-but-valid body before the body deadline 98ms\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  14 passed (14)\n```\n\n### Loopback proof\n\n- **Body drip fail-closed**: real `http.createServer` peer returns HTTP 200 then drips 1 byte every 40ms; with `bodyTimeoutMs: 250`, real `fetch` + real `downloadLineMedia` rejects with `\"LINE media body for message mid-drip timed out after 0.25 seconds\"`, elapsed ~692ms — bounded, not an indefinite hang.\n- **Slow-but-valid success**: same loopback path with an 80ms paced body and `bodyTimeoutMs: 1500` completes with `size: 2` — healthy slow transfer is not false-killed.\n- **Readiness unchanged**: hung pre-header fetch still rejects with `\"did not become ready within 15 seconds\"`; readiness `AbortSignal` aborts; `saveMediaStream` is not called.\n- **Separate budgets**: drip-after-headers abort uses the **body** error string while the readiness signal stays un-aborted; late readiness (~14s 202 hang) + 1.5s slow-valid body still succeeds under a fresh 2s body budget (would fail a shared 15s total).\n\n### Not tested\n\nLive `api-data.line.me` with LINE channel credentials — requires real LINE bot token in this contributor environment.",
